rule case_routing v1
description "Which reviewer a new case goes to. Each reviewer who is in today takes cases in proportion to their capacity: one number is drawn below the total of the capacities of those in, and the reviewer whose share it falls in takes the case. With nobody in, the case waits (reviewer 0). An example written for the purpose"

enum presence = away | in_office

# One reviewer of the team. The caller passes the whole team, in a fixed order
elements reviewers
  reviewer_id : number  range >=1 <=50
  present     : bool
  capacity    : number  range >=0 <=100

inputs
  roll : number  range >=0 <=9999  random  # drawn below the total of the capacities of those in

outputs
  reviewer : number  round down(1)  # 0 when nobody is in

table in_today
policy unique
| present | -> presence : presence |
| true    | in_office              |
| false   | away                   |

# A reviewer who is in takes the case with the chance of their capacity over the total of the
# capacities of those in.
fold presence over reviewers
  away      -> next
  in_office -> take_weighted reviewer_id by capacity
  empty     -> 0
  exhausted -> held

sequence team_of_three
| reviewer_id | present | capacity |
| 1           | true    | 50       |
| 2           | true    | 30       |
| 3           | true    | 20       |

sequence first_away
| reviewer_id | present | capacity |
| 1           | false   | 50       |
| 2           | true    | 30       |
| 3           | true    | 20       |

sequence nobody_in
| reviewer_id | present | capacity |
| 1           | false   | 50       |

sequence no_reviewers
| reviewer_id | present | capacity |

chances
| reviewers     | -> reviewer | chance |
| team_of_three | 1           | 1/2    |
| team_of_three | 2           | 3/10   |
| team_of_three | 3           | 1/5    |
| first_away    | 1           | 0      |
| first_away    | 2           | 3/5    |
| nobody_in     | 0           | 1      |
| no_reviewers  | 0           | 1      |

examples
| roll | reviewers     | -> reviewer |
| 0    | team_of_three | 1           |
| 49   | team_of_three | 1           |
| 50   | team_of_three | 2           |
| 79   | team_of_three | 2           |
| 80   | team_of_three | 3           |
| 0    | first_away    | 2           |
| 30   | first_away    | 3           |
| 0    | no_reviewers  | 0           |
